# The runtime's doubles as text and text as doubles, held to IEEE 754 and to
# the runtime's words: show_f64's digits judged on the exact interval of the reals
# that round to the double, its layout, str_to_double against the C
# library's strtod, to_int, and ownership (doubles.cpp states each), on
# doubles that include IEEE 754's words (signed zeros, infinities, NaNs of
# every payload), subnormals, ties and the integer edges 2^53, 2^62, 2^63
# and 2^64. Each run draws from a fresh seed, which a failure names; then
# each check runs with its own planted fault and must catch it. One line
# per property; the classes each reached go to the report.
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
. "$root/harness/prop/prop.sh"
prop_build "$here/doubles.cpp" "$work/doubles" || exit 0
# The case count is debt: 1000 cases took 3 s on an arm64 Mac (host clang,
# -O1); set it on the owner's build so the program ends well within
# step_limit on both targets.
prop_run "$work/doubles" --cases 1000
